WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.157
Two law students can receive the same score for different
reasons.

2
00:00:05.157 --> 00:00:10.423
One remembers the words. Another understands the idea but
misses a key condition.

3
00:00:10.423 --> 00:00:14.880
LexLearn starts with these differences, then builds a personal
learning path.

4
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.306
The journey begins with a short diagnostic. Students read a
legal provision, answer questions,

5
00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:28.112
and explain what they remember in their own words. This
separates recall from understanding

6
00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:31.430
and identifies a useful starting point for practice.

7
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:38.773
Recall and understanding are shown separately. Together with
evidence about legal precision and answer

8
00:00:38.773 --> 00:00:44.513
structure, they help describe the student's current needs. This
cognitive profile guides the next

9
00:00:44.513 --> 00:00:48.613
step. It is a starting point, not a permanent label.

10
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:55.250
The student then follows a six week path with thirty practice
sessions.

11
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.431
Each stage combines focused tasks, retrieval, spaced review,
and feedback.

12
00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:05.283
Completed work opens the next step, while confirmed assessment
evidence helps guide later practice.

13
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.379
During a session, students retrieve a rule, explain its
meaning, and apply it to

14
00:01:12.379 --> 00:01:16.685
a changed situation. The relevant country, law, and article
remain visible.

15
00:01:16.685 --> 00:01:20.990
Short, clear steps help first year law students organize their
reasoning.

16
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.495
After an answer, feedback shows what was supported and what
still needs attention.

17
00:01:27.495 --> 00:01:32.014
Students can compare their response with the reference and try
another task.

18
00:01:32.014 --> 00:01:35.780
The aim is a clear, manageable next step in learning.

19
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:43.332
The personal legal dictionary explains terms with simple
examples. Students can also choose a

20
00:01:43.332 --> 00:01:47.993
role they would like to explore: judge, lawyer, or university
professor.

21
00:01:47.993 --> 00:01:52.230
Their choice helps connect the learning experience with their
interests.

22
00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:58.648
As students move through the stages, recall and understanding
remain separate.

23
00:01:58.648 --> 00:02:04.351
The final review brings the journey together. Sample figures in
this video illustrate the

24
00:02:04.351 --> 00:02:09.647
interface only. They are not real student records or proof of
learning gains.

25
00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:15.315
Supervisors can follow progress and see areas that need
attention.

26
00:02:15.315 --> 00:02:20.983
Human review supports more focused academic guidance. Students
receive a simpler view of their

27
00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:26.247
own progress, with the next step connected to the work they
have completed.

28
00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:33.293
From the first diagnostic to guided practice and the final
review, LexLearn connects the

29
00:02:33.293 --> 00:02:37.556
learning journey. We understand how you think, then build your
path.

30
00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:40.657
Explore the working platform at lexlearnsmart dot com.
